-- title:
--   Absolute irreducibility at level prime to p
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $N$ a non-zero natural number and $S$ a finite set of natural numbers with $p \in S$ and containing every prime divisor of $N$; let $\mathcal{O}'$ be a discrete valuation domain of characteristic zero, adically complete for its maximal ideal and with finite residue field, such that the image of $p$ lies in its maximal ideal, and let $K$ be a fraction field of $\mathcal{O}'$. Let $\chi$ be a ring homomorphism to $\mathcal{O}'$ from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}} S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the operators `heckeTLin` for primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$ together with the operators `heckeULin` for primes $q \mid N$ with $q \notin S$, and assume $p \nmid N$. Let $\rho$ be a [`GaloisRepAdic`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L16) over $\mathcal{O}'$: a finite free $\mathcal{O}'$-module $V$ of rank $2$ with a monoid homomorphism $\rho$ from $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$, realised as the $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphisms of `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, to $\operatorname{End}_{\mathcal{O}'}(V)$, which is adically continuous in the sense that for every $n$ there is a finite extension $L/\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\rho(\sigma)v - v \in \mathfrak{m}^n V$ for all $v \in V$ and all $\sigma$ fixing $L$ pointwise. Assume further that for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$ and $\ell \notin S$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit of $A$, and every $\sigma$ that is a Frobenius at $\ell$ for $A$ (that is, $\sigma$ lies in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and acts on the residue field of $A$ by $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$), one has $\operatorname{charpoly}(\rho(\sigma)) = X^2 - \chi(T_\ell)X + \ell$. The conclusion is that the $K$-span of the set of base-changed endomorphisms $\rho(\sigma) \otimes K$, for $\sigma$ ranging over the Galois group, is the whole of $\operatorname{End}_K(K \otimes_{\mathcal{O}'} V)$.
--
--   This is Ribet's irreducibility theorem for the two-dimensional $p$-adic representations attached to a point of the weight-two cuspidal Hecke algebra, in the case of level prime to $p$, stated in the Burnside form (the Galois image spans the full endomorphism algebra after passage to the fraction field) and for an arbitrary representation whose Frobenius characteristic polynomials are prescribed by $\chi$ rather than only for the representation constructed from an eigenform. It is used in the proof of [`CuspForm.isFlatAt_of_point_of_not_dvd`](thm.html#CuspForm.isFlatAt_of_point_of_not_dvd).
